        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "[codex] fix(sessions): report archive cleanup in sessions cleanup",
        "body": "Fixes #75658\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\n`openclaw sessions cleanup --dry-run` did not preview stale `.deleted.*` and `.reset.*` archive files, and the apply summary did not report when those physical archive files were removed. Operators could see only unreferenced-artifact counts even when deleted/reset session archives were the files consuming disk.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe cleanup command already had an archive retention helper, but dry-run did not call it and store maintenance discarded its removal count. This change reuses the existing archive-retention rules for both preview and apply reporting instead of adding a second cleanup policy.\n\nReviewer follow-up: dry-run archive cleanup now accepts an exclusion set, and the sessions cleanup preview passes in the disk-budget simulated removal paths. A stale archive already claimed by disk-budget cleanup is therefore not counted again as deleted/reset archive cleanup.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers running `sessions cleanup` now see deleted/reset archive cleanup in dry-run output and in apply output. Forced cleanup also scans the store directory for stale deleted archives even when no session rows were removed, while `resetArchiveRetention: false` still preserves reset archives.\n\n## Evidence\n\nFocused validation:\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/config/sessions/store.pruning.integration.test.ts src/commands/sessions-cleanup.test.ts src/gateway/session-transcript-files.fs.archive-cleanup.test.ts`\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs test/scripts/check-session-accessor-boundary.test.ts`\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/config/sessions/store.pruning.test.ts`\n- `git diff --check`\n\nReal CLI proof, with temp paths redacted:\n\n```text\n$ node --import tsx src/entry.ts --no-color sessions cleanup --store \"$TMP/archive-store/sessions.json\" --dry-run --enforce\nSession store: $TMP/archive-store/sessions.json\nMaintenance mode: enforce\nEntries: 0 -> 0 (remove 0)\nWould prune missing transcripts: 0\nWould retire stale direct DM sessions: 0\nWould prune stale model-run probes: 0\nWould prune stale: 0\nWould cap overflow: 0\nWould prune deleted/reset archives: 2\nWould prune unreferenced artifacts: 0\n\nafter dry-run files:\n[\"fresh.jsonl.deleted.2026-06-26T00-00-00.000Z\",\"redacted-deleted.jsonl.deleted.2026-01-01T00-00-00.000Z\",\"redacted-reset.jsonl.reset.2026-01-01T00-00-00.000Z\",\"sessions.json\"]\n\n$ node --import tsx src/entry.ts --no-color sessions cleanup --store \"$TMP/archive-store/sessions.json\" --enforce\nSession store: $TMP/archive-store/sessions.json\nApplied maintenance. Current entries: 0\nPruned deleted/reset archives: 2\n\nafter apply files:\n[\"fresh.jsonl.deleted.2026-06-26T00-00-00.000Z\",\"sessions.json\"]\n```\n\nDisk-budget double-count proof from the same CLI command in JSON mode, with `maxDiskBytes: 1000` and one oversized stale archive:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"archiveCleanup\": {\n    \"scannedFiles\": 0,\n    \"removedFiles\": 0\n  },\n  \"diskBudget\": {\n    \"removedFiles\": 1,\n    \"totalBytesBefore\": 2085,\n    \"totalBytesAfter\": 85\n  }\n}\n```\n\nNot run:\n\n- `codex review --base origin/main` was attempted, but the local approval policy rejected the command because it would export the unpublished diff/repository context to an external service.\n\n## AI Assistance\n\nAI-assisted: yes. I used Codex to inspect the issue, avoid duplicate PRs, implement the patch, and run the focused validation above.\n",
